       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose for oral ibuprofen.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg/day. The maximum for prescription use in adults is 3200 mg/day, so this is twice that. Over-the-counter labeling caps it at 1200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove these risks.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1600 mg total per day, which may be where the \"1600\" came from\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is intended and there's a clinical reason for it. I'll enter the order once that's settled."
      }
     ],
